===== path show
Show a single session as a markdown summary (used by fzf preview)

Usage: path show [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  claude    Show a Claude conversation as a markdown summary
  gemini    Show a Gemini CLI conversation as a markdown summary
  codex     Show a Codex CLI session as a markdown summary
  copilot   Show a GitHub Copilot CLI session as a markdown summary (preview)
  opencode  Show an opencode session as a markdown summary
  cursor    Show a Cursor composer as a markdown summary
  pi        Show a Pi (pi.dev) session as a markdown summary
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --ansi
          Emit ANSI-styled terminal output instead of raw markdown (bold speakers, dim metadata, colored diffs). Used by the fzf preview panes

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
===== path show claude
Show a Claude conversation as a markdown summary

Usage: path show claude [OPTIONS] --project <PROJECT> --session <SESSION>

Options:
  -p, --project <PROJECT>
          Project path (e.g., /Users/alex/myproject)

  -s, --session <SESSION>
          Session id (the file stem of the JSONL)

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
